WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.250
Step seven dry-runs the plan
with its approved hash.

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.562
It would send four writes, in order.

3
00:00:05.562 --> 00:00:09.812
First, Disable A D Account for
conversion one's legacy account.

4
00:00:09.812 --> 00:00:11.587
Disabled, not deleted.

5
00:00:11.587 --> 00:00:15.263
Then a post of an application's
federated credential to Graph.

6
00:00:15.263 --> 00:00:18.715
Then a put of the user-assigned
identity, id webfront,

7
00:00:18.715 --> 00:00:22.087
to Resource Manager, before
a put of its credential.

8
00:00:22.087 --> 00:00:26.624
The identity always comes before
its credential, one write at a time.

9
00:00:26.624 --> 00:00:31.800
Step eight applies the plan to the fake,
and all four are sent, in the same order.

10
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:36.725
Then it tries a hash nobody approved,
all zeros, and the write path refuses:

11
00:00:36.725 --> 00:00:41.650
the plan's hash isn't the approved one,
so it won't run a plan nobody reviewed.

12
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:46.663
Step nine runs every test: five
hundred thirteen pass, none fail.

13
00:00:46.663 --> 00:00:48.550
Then delete the output folder.
